1
00:00:13,270 --> 00:00:14,130
Chu Mingke

2
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:29,030
Your Highness.

3
00:00:29,030 --> 00:00:30,000
The bleeding won't stop.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,670
He has lost too much blood.

5
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,630
The wound powder

6
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:33,200
is washed away as soon as we apply it.

7
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:33,770
Useless.

8
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:34,700
All of you are useless.

9
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:36,400
What use are you to me?

10
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:36,900
Where is the imperial physician?

11
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,470
Did I not send for him?

12
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:39,900
Where is the physician?

13
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,630
Your Highness, the physician is here.

14
00:00:46,570 --> 00:00:47,870
Huabai! Huabai!

15
00:00:48,030 --> 00:00:49,030
The physician is here.

16
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:50,670
Now that the physician is here, you can be
saved.

17
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:51,730
Hold on.

18
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:03,570
Stop.

19
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:04,530
How dare you!

20
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,830
Can't you see my brother is bleeding nonstop?

21
00:01:06,830 --> 00:01:08,470
The physician should be treating my brother.

22
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,430
Where do you think you are going?

23
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,600
Your Highness.

24
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,070
The Director is unconscious.

25
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:14,430
He is barely hanging on by a thread.

26
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:16,530
My lord, please examine our Director first.

27
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,130
Our young master has lost so much blood.

28
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:19,130
We cannot stop it.

29
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:19,930
If the physician does not come soon,

30
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:21,270
he may bleed dry.

31
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,870
My brother's life is in danger.

32
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,300
If you stand by and let him die,

33
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,800
if anything happens to him, I will have you
buried with him.

34
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,000
Bring the physician in at once.

35
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,830
Or must I invite him myself?

36
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:31,800
Physician, this way, please.

37
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,700
He is clearly the reason my brother is bleeding
like this.

38
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:36,830
Who allowed you to treat him?

39
00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:38,030
When the horse lost control,

40
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:40,100
the Director stood between His Majesty and us.

41
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:41,670
If not for him risking his life to protect His
Majesty,

42
00:01:41,729 --> 00:01:43,600
we would be the ones lying here now.

43
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:44,229
I...

44
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:45,729
And you.

45
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:47,630
You asked to let your brother tame the horse,

46
00:01:47,729 --> 00:01:49,700
yet that horse charged at His Majesty.

47
00:01:49,770 --> 00:01:52,170
Now the Director is on the brink of death after
saving His Majesty,

48
00:01:52,170 --> 00:01:53,729
and you refuse to let the physician save him.

49
00:01:53,830 --> 00:01:55,530
I should be the one asking that question,

50
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:56,130
Consort Chen.

51
00:01:56,170 --> 00:01:57,870
What exactly are you scheming?

52
00:01:57,870 --> 00:02:00,430
You... Even if he wanted to stop that horse,

53
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:01,870
he should not have injured my brother.

54
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:03,070
Even if he had cut off the horse's head,

55
00:02:03,270 --> 00:02:04,500
its body would still have surged forward.

56
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:06,030
Without the Director's move to save His Majesty,

57
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:07,300
how else could the horse have been stopped?

58
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:08,970
What is your brother worth?

59
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:11,230
Should His Majesty's sacred body be harmed for
his sake?

60
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:14,130
You... You are all in league with each other.

61
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:15,100
You are all...

62
00:02:15,130 --> 00:02:15,800
all doing this for...

63
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:17,130
His Majesty has arrived!

64
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:21,329
Long live Your Majesty!

65
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:24,770
Your Majesty.

66
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:25,900
My brother...

67
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:26,530
I...

68
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:29,870
Summon Imperial Physician Zhang for questioning.

69
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:31,670
Your Majesty.

70
00:02:32,329 --> 00:02:33,329
You may leave first.

71
00:02:36,970 --> 00:02:37,770
Yes.

72
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:44,870
Rise, all of you.

73
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:45,300
Sit.

74
00:02:45,329 --> 00:02:45,800
Yes.

75
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,170
How is the Director?

76
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:53,470
Reporting to Your Majesty, the Director's pulse
is chaotic.

77
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,670
It seems his internal organs have been injured.

78
00:02:54,670 --> 00:02:56,270
He also shows signs of bleeding from the seven
orifices.

79
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:57,370
I fear his head may be injured as well.

80
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,329
Then... how should he be treated?

81
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,030
Although the Director was struck by the wild
horse,

82
00:03:01,170 --> 00:03:02,070
and suffered a shock to the head,

83
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,630
I have used methods to calm the rising yang and
settle the wind,

84
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:06,000
stabilizing the disorder in his qi and blood.

85
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:08,570
He only needs a few days of quiet rest.

86
00:03:10,370 --> 00:03:11,170
My child.

87
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:12,230
Your Highness.

88
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:13,600
I must thank you.

89
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:14,930
You saved his life.

90
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
No thanks are needed, Your Highness.

91
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:18,500
Your identity is special.

92
00:03:18,670 --> 00:03:19,900
It is not convenient for you to stay here long.

93
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,000
You should return first.

94
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:22,329
Yes.

95
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:32,500
Gerile.

96
00:03:32,630 --> 00:03:33,970
You are the one the Khan has chosen.

97
00:03:34,329 --> 00:03:35,470
Your status is noble now.

98
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:36,329
Things are no longer as they were before.

99
00:03:36,570 --> 00:03:38,370
Why risk yourself for someone from the Central
Plains?

100
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,930
This was not a risk.

101
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,329
Let me warn you.

102
00:03:42,730 --> 00:03:43,930
If anything happens to you,

103
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,470
everything will be ruined.

104
00:03:47,570 --> 00:03:48,870
Are you not still here?

105
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:50,900
The Khan sent you here

106
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:53,500
to guard against an accident like me, did he
not?

107
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:54,100
You...

108
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:55,700
Do not think I do not know

109
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:57,370
why you truly came here.

110
00:03:58,700 --> 00:03:59,300
Do not forget.

111
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:01,170
Your Ata's body is still at the royal court.

112
00:04:01,370 --> 00:04:02,470
By the Wolf God above,

113
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,170
if you dare betray the Khan,

114
00:04:04,170 --> 00:04:06,530
he will make sure your Ata's soul never rests.

115
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:09,300
Where are you going?

116
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:11,370
That is none of your concern.

117
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:13,570
A lowborn wretch born a slave.

118
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,899
It is freezing, after all.

119
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:24,700
These slaves are not as quick as they used to
be.

120
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:28,600
Guess how many will be left in the end.

121
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,830
I bet not a single one.

122
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:31,730
It has been snowing for half a month.

123
00:04:31,970 --> 00:04:33,930
Who knows how long the wolves in the hunting
ground have been starving?

124
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:36,030
These slaves will barely be enough to fill their
teeth.

125
00:04:36,030 --> 00:04:37,300
Do not speak too soon.

126
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:37,600
What?

127
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:38,830
You do not believe me?

128
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:40,500
Then I will wager my best horse,

129
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,170
plus three fine wolf pelts,

130
00:04:42,170 --> 00:04:44,100
that these slaves will be eaten to the last one.

131
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:45,270
Dare to bet?

132
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,830
Why would I not?

133
00:04:48,230 --> 00:04:49,630
Then I will stake ten sheep

134
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:51,800
and the rare wine granted by the Khan

135
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:54,170
that at least one slave will hunt a wolf and
return alive.

136
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:56,130
Do not go back on your word when the time comes.

137
00:04:58,230 --> 00:04:59,100
I am in too.

138
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:19,400
Go. My wound is too severe.

139
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:20,900
Taking me with you will only slow you down.

140
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,230
Stop talking. Save your strength.

141
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,800
I am getting you out of here.

142
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,100
No. We have hunted nothing.

143
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:27,800
Even if we get out, we will not survive.

144
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:31,270
The wolves are following us.

145
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:36,770
Stay behind me. Do not move.

146
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:42,500
Watch out!

147
00:05:45,030 --> 00:05:46,900
Get away! Get away!

148
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,870
Wuen!

149
00:05:50,470 --> 00:05:51,770
Survive.

150
00:05:54,670 --> 00:05:55,770
Go away!

151
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:04,670
The sun is about to set.

152
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,770
I am afraid there are no survivors.

153
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,570
A bet is a bet. Pay up.

154
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,770
A bunch of useless trash.

155
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:17,900
Wait. What is that? Someone is there.

156
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,200
Someone is still alive.

157
00:06:20,430 --> 00:06:21,230
Really?

158
00:06:28,870 --> 00:06:30,900
Turtan, did I not tell you?

159
00:06:31,070 --> 00:06:33,200
It is still too early to say who wins and who
loses.

160
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:36,100
You lowly beast.

161
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,300
You made me lose the bet.

162
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,100
Damn you.

163
00:06:39,930 --> 00:06:40,730
Damn you!

164
00:06:46,470 --> 00:06:47,800
What are you doing?

165
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:50,030
General Bilige.

166
00:06:50,370 --> 00:06:52,900
We are selecting the bravest slave.

167
00:06:53,770 --> 00:06:55,170
The bravest slave?

168
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:58,170
You are going to beat the brave slave to death?

169
00:06:58,230 --> 00:06:59,300
Whose slave is this?

170
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,430
He belongs to Turtan's family.

171
00:07:00,430 --> 00:07:02,000
Go back and tell your Ata

172
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:02,900
that this slave

173
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:04,230
has been bought by me, Bilige.

174
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,270
From now on, you will be called Gerile.

175
00:07:07,470 --> 00:07:08,770
I will be your Ata.

176
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,130
Mingke injured his head?

177
00:07:16,230 --> 00:07:17,230
Do not worry, Your Majesty.

178
00:07:17,330 --> 00:07:18,730
I examined him carefully.

179
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:19,730
Aside from the external wounds,

180
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:21,070
there is no hidden injury to his head.

181
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:22,300
The Director rendered great service by saving
Your Majesty.

182
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,730
He is blessed by fortune.

183
00:07:24,570 --> 00:07:25,200
Saved me...

184
00:07:37,370 --> 00:07:38,170
Your Majesty.

185
00:07:40,770 --> 00:07:41,800
Your Majesty,

186
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,930
please take care of yourself.

187
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:47,600
I am fine.

188
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:49,830
Will Mingke's injury leave any lingering
effects?

189
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:51,200
The Director's injuries are not severe.

190
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,600
As long as he rests well,

191
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,670
and avoids exhausting himself,

192
00:07:53,670 --> 00:07:54,570
he will surely recover.

193
00:07:56,230 --> 00:07:56,930
In that case,

194
00:07:57,230 --> 00:07:59,270
have Mingke sent back first.

195
00:07:59,530 --> 00:08:00,970
Let him recuperate properly for a few days.

196
00:08:02,830 --> 00:08:04,000
You may withdraw as well.

197
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:05,630
Yes.

198
00:08:13,230 --> 00:08:13,830
Lindeng.

199
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:15,030
This old servant is here.

200
00:08:15,530 --> 00:08:16,770
Pass down my order.

201
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:18,870
Break camp at once. We return to the palace.

202
00:08:19,130 --> 00:08:19,830
Yes.

203
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:29,270
He looks more and more like him.

204
00:08:31,370 --> 00:08:32,630
Congratulations on Your Majesty's ascension.

205
00:08:32,630 --> 00:08:34,429
Why have you started speaking such formal words
too?

206
00:08:34,429 --> 00:08:34,900
What is this?

207
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:35,900
Now that I have ascended the throne,

208
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,130
will you become distant from me?

209
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,100
It is not distance.

210
00:08:38,230 --> 00:08:39,370
It is the loyalty of a subject.

211
00:08:39,370 --> 00:08:41,030
Your Majesty, though I am unworthy,

212
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:42,330
I will give everything I have

213
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,200
to clear every obstacle from Your Majesty's
path.

214
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:44,970
I will never leave or abandon you.

215
00:08:44,970 --> 00:08:45,970
In life and death, I will follow you.

216
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:47,970
The criminal official Shan Muchuan

217
00:08:48,070 --> 00:08:49,000
colluded with a foreign enemy.

218
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,170
His entire clan shall be executed.

219
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:52,970
Your Majesty, why do you not believe me?

220
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:51,300
Who is there?

221
00:09:54,230 --> 00:09:55,600
My lord, I came to see you.
